00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:43.170
So last time, we talked about
Boltzmann transport equation,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.840
and we made a drastic
approximation.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.000
That's a relaxation
time approximation.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.490
So using this relaxation
time approximation,

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:01.650
the original Boltzmann
transport equation,

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.650
on the right-hand side
was a scattering term.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:10.650
If you recall, we said that
it's the [INAUDIBLE] right?

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.170
Because we say, when we
have two particles colliding

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.760
with each other, we have to
sum up all the possibilities

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.770
for the collision.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:24.450
But using the relaxation
time approximation,

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.750
we say all those
collisions eventually

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.350
drive the system back
to an equilibrium F0.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:37.630
So that F0 is the equivalent
distribution function.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:41.890
And we also
commented-- actually,

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.210
this is not really strict.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.060
This is, of course,
a approximation.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.140
There are many ways
it's not correct.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:56.470
And later on, you'll see that,
in fact, this approximation

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.670
will not give you the right
[INAUDIBLE] when you calculate

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:03.550
the fluid properties.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:10.090
And for relaxation time, we
discuss different scattering

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:15.850
mechanisms, for example, phonon
scattering, electron phonon

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:20.110
scattering, and
scattering by impurities.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:24.220
And we say, if I have multiple
scattering mechanisms,

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.850
I use the methods and rule
where the total relaxation

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:35.320
time is the inverse of all the
scattering processes involved

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.870
in the transport.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.650
And I want to also make
the additional comment

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:45.010
that, even though, you
can solve the Boltzmann

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.080
equation in this format on the
relaxation time approximation.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.870
And often, the
largest uncertainty

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.450
come from this relaxation time.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:01.360
We do not have a good way to
calculate relaxation time.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.960
We say you go to quantum
mechanical Fermi,

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.090
say Golden rule to
calculate, so that way you

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.220
have to go to quantum mechanics.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:16.670
